Z||000000||Greg Piet||10-01-2000||10:01 PM||||OK I am being a sore loser...<BR>I am in the C-stock category with ym Fiero...<P>I beat everyone with "normal" tires.  There is a guy who has a Miata with Kuhmo's with a 50 treadwear on it...   Now on todays track all the C-stock cars were bunched up around 100 seconds ( I won against the next fastest car by only .1 seconds.)...  This guy beat us all by 10 seconds.  I do not see how a 50 treadwear tire can be considered  "in the spirit of stock"  <P>Well I thought I saw on the website a rule that stated tires in the stock category must be treadwear 140 or higher.  I cannot find it now!   Does anyone know if this is a dream or a real rule (SCCA Fiero???)?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PJ||10-02-2000||10:21 AM||||Ten years ago it was any DOT tire could be used and I don't think the rules have changed.<P>Treadwear numbers on the sidewalls are decided by the manufacturer with no strict rules or inforced industry-wide standards. Example: Hoosier DOT race radials have a treadwear number of 0! I don't think Denver whould write a rule based on arbitrary info supplied by the makers, but then again...<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<P>PS When the '88 Fiero was dominant in C-Stock nationally I remember them running 205/60's all around. Sticky (for the time) BFGs and Yoko's.<BR>||||reg||1
